            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdominal pain: the importance of genital examination.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>398-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Torsion of an intra-abdominal testis is a rare cause of acute abdominal pain. The purpose of this report is to highlight a case of torsion of an abdominal testis in a patient with an unusual clinical presentation, with the fortuitous diagnosis of a &quot;carcinoma in situ&quot; and to emphasize the role of routine genital examination when investigating patients with abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
